[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omec-project/smf/issues/comments/4605753053","html_url":"https://github.com/omec-project/smf/issues/548#issuecomment-4605753053","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omec-project/smf/issues/548","id":4605753053,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEvOtfs8AAAABEoY23Q","user":{"login":"gab-arrobo","id":87488727,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDg4NzI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87488727?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo","html_url":"https://github.com/gab-arrobo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-02T18:18:37Z","updated_at":"2026-06-02T18:18:37Z","body":"Sorry, I just noticed this issue :-(\n\n> ## Question for maintainers\n> Before I open the PR I’d like to check:\n> \n> * Does the framing (defensive retry + cache-bypass re-discovery + DB-recovery rebuild) make sense to you, or would you prefer a different approach (e.g. removing the per-SMContext `CommunicationClient` entirely and looking up via the NRF cache on every call)?\n\nThe approach makes sense. However, I think that it will add latency because of the lookup on every N1N2 transfer\n\n> * Are you happy with the change being a single commit, or would you prefer it split (e.g. `RebuildCommunicationClient` + DB recovery as one PR, retry/timeout/re-discovery as a follow-up)?\n\nI think a single commit is fine because the solution seems tightly coupled\n\n> * Any preference on whether unit tests should accompany this fix, or is it acceptable to ship without (similar to recent fix-style PRs)?\n\nNot sure about unit tests. Do not we need the entire 5GC deployed to be able to replicate the issue and solution?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omec-project/smf/issues/comments/4605753053/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omec-project/smf/issues/comments/4622589786","html_url":"https://github.com/omec-project/smf/issues/548#issuecomment-4622589786","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omec-project/smf/issues/548","id":4622589786,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEvOtfs8AAAABE4cfWg","user":{"login":"donivtech","id":160624796,"node_id":"U_kgDOCZLwnA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/160624796?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/donivtech","html_url":"https://github.com/donivtech","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/donivtech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/donivtech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/donivtech/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/donivtech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/donivtech/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/donivtech/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/donivtech/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/donivtech/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/donivtech/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-04T13:28:49Z","updated_at":"2026-06-04T13:28:49Z","body":"Thanks Gabriel, quick clarification on the latency: the PR keeps the per-SMContext CommunicationClient and uses it directly on the happy path. The NRF lookup only fires after a HTTP failure on the cached client, and the only steady-state change is a 5s context.WithTimeout ceiling. My Q1 wording was ambiguous — the \"lookup on every call\" was a  hypothetical counter-design, not what #549 does.\n  \nOn the tests, you're right that reproducing the bug end-to-end needs a full 5GC deployed with an AMF pod restart (which is how we verified it on test clusters). On the other two: keeping it as a single commit, and happy to add a couple of unit tests for the helpers (RebuildCommunicationClient and the candidate-iteration logic) in a  follow-up if you'd like them, otherwise I'll leave it test-free as per recent fix-style PRs.\n\nOne ask: PR #549 only has DCO so far — could you kick off the rest of the CI workflows when you get a chance? Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omec-project/smf/issues/comments/4622589786/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omec-project/smf/issues/comments/4624771001","html_url":"https://github.com/omec-project/smf/issues/548#issuecomment-4624771001","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omec-project/smf/issues/548","id":4624771001,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEvOtfs8AAAABE6hnuQ","user":{"login":"gab-arrobo","id":87488727,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NDg4NzI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87488727?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo","html_url":"https://github.com/gab-arrobo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gab-arrobo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url"